WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:06.536
Look at a goat, and look at a stone.

2
00:00:06.756 --> 00:00:09.543
One of them is alive. One was never alive.

3
00:00:10.043 --> 00:00:12.318
Is a goat alive? Let us check four things.

4
00:00:12.538 --> 00:00:17.786
One. It grows. A baby goat, called
a kid, grows into a big goat.

5
00:00:18.006 --> 00:00:20.607
Two. It needs food, so it eats grass.

6
00:00:20.827 --> 00:00:23.195
Three. It needs water, so it drinks.

7
00:00:23.415 --> 00:00:28.245
Four. It can have young. A goat
has baby goats, called kids.

8
00:00:28.465 --> 00:00:33.573
Anything that grows, needs food and
water, and can have young is alive.

9
00:00:34.073 --> 00:00:36.952
Now look at a stone. Does it grow? No.

10
00:00:37.172 --> 00:00:41.027
Does it need food or water?
No. Can it have young? No.

11
00:00:41.247 --> 00:00:46.587
A stone was never alive. Neither
was a spoon, a car or a teddy bear.

12
00:00:46.807 --> 00:00:51.173
A car moves, but it was never
alive. Moving is not the test.

13
00:00:51.673 --> 00:00:56.642
A cat is an animal. Every animal
needs three things to stay alive.

14
00:00:56.862 --> 00:01:00.670
Air to breathe. Water to
drink. And the right food.

15
00:01:00.890 --> 00:01:05.302
A cat does not need a ball of wool.
It wants one. That is different.

16
00:01:05.522 --> 00:01:09.980
You are an animal too. You need air,
water and food, just like the cat.

17
00:01:10.480 --> 00:01:14.613
Plants are alive too. A
seed grows into a new plant.

18
00:01:14.833 --> 00:01:19.338
Plants do not eat like animals. They
make their own food in their leaves.

19
00:01:19.558 --> 00:01:21.973
To make it, they use light from the Sun.

20
00:01:22.193 --> 00:01:27.626
They need water from the soil, and air.
They take in water through their roots.

21
00:01:27.846 --> 00:01:31.701
Today you will find out what
happens to a plant with no water.

22
00:01:32.201 --> 00:01:35.869
How can you find out? Take
two plants that are the same.

23
00:01:36.089 --> 00:01:39.805
Water one every day. Give
the other no water at all.

24
00:01:40.025 --> 00:01:43.693
Only the water is different.
That makes it a fair test.

25
00:01:43.913 --> 00:01:50.183
First, you predict: say what you think
will happen. It is fine to be wrong.

26
00:01:50.403 --> 00:01:54.118
Then you watch for five days,
and see what really happens.

27
00:01:54.618 --> 00:02:00.609
A scientist looks closely, asks a question,
tries something, and writes down what happened.

28
00:02:00.829 --> 00:02:04.497
You will write what you see in
a table, so you do not forget.

29
00:02:04.717 --> 00:02:08.154
Then you say what happened, and
if it matched your prediction.

30
00:02:08.654 --> 00:02:13.716
A goat is alive. It grows, needs
food and water, and has young.

31
00:02:13.936 --> 00:02:18.766
A stone was never alive. Animals
need air, water and the right food.

32
00:02:18.986 --> 00:02:22.747
Plants need water from the
soil, and light from the Sun.

33
00:02:22.967 --> 00:02:28.540
A scientist looks, asks, tries and
writes it down. Ready? Let us go.
